{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And it shall be for him and his seed after him etc.</b> That he be anointed for war from here onward, and thus is it said: ״במלחמת מדין אותם ואת פנחס בן אלעזר הכהן לצבא וכו״. From here our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said that Phinehas was not consecrated as priest until he killed Zimri. And with this is resolved what the world asks: how did Phinehas kill Zimri and become impure through a corpse? For one may say that until now the priesthood was given only to Aaron and his sons, but not to his sons' sons; and also in the inauguration you find it written: ״לאהרן ולבניו תעשה כתנות״ — and not to his sons' sons. And furthermore one may say that he left Zimri as a goses and he did not actually die, and a goses does not impart impurity. And on this did Rabbi Samuel object: but from the eighth day of the inauguration Phinehas was already anointed for war, for this rejoicing is counted among the seven rejoicings — that Elisheva wife of Aaron was distinguished above the others, for the son of her son was anointed for war. But perhaps from there he was given to be anointed for war, but for the service and for generations, no. And here the priesthood was given to him for all matters, and to his seed after him: a covenant of everlasting priesthood." "<b>And he atoned for the children of Israel.</b> And it is fitting to make other atonements."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:16.485428587Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}